{
  "info": {
    "name": "Market Propiedades - API",
    "description": "Colección para probar el backend local. El login guarda el token automáticamente en la variable {{accessToken}}, así las requests siguientes lo usan solas.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3002" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "adminEmail", "value": "marco.silvaponce10@gmail.com" },
    { "key": "adminPassword", "value": "cambia-esta-contrasena-min-8-chars" },
    { "key": "comunaId", "value": "13501" },
    { "key": "publicadorId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "propertyId", "value": "" },
    { "key": "propertySlug", "value": "" },
    { "key": "fotoId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (correcto)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Si las credenciales son correctas, devuelve { accessToken }. El script de Tests (pestaña abajo en Postman) guarda ese token en la variable de colección para las demás requests."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve accessToken', () => pm.expect(body.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "",
                  "if (body.accessToken) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', body.accessToken);",
                  "  console.log('Token guardado en {{accessToken}}');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (password incorrecta)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"password-que-no-es\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/login", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "login"] },
            "description": "Mismo endpoint, contraseña mala a propósito. Tiene que devolver 401 con el mismo mensaje genérico que si el email tampoco existiera."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 401', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me (con token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "auth": {
              "type": "bearer",
              "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }]
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] },
            "description": "Usa el token guardado por 'Login (correcto)'. Corré esa primero. Devuelve el usuario que JwtStrategy encontró en la base a partir del `sub` del token."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 200', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('Devuelve el email correcto', () => {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().email).to.eql(pm.collectionVariables.get('adminEmail'));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Me (sin token)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/me", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "me"] },
            "description": "A propósito sin Authorization header. Tiene que devolver 401 — JwtAuthGuard corta antes de llegar al controller."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 401 sin token', () => pm.response.to.have.status(401));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Users (publicadores)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Crear corredora de prueba",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"paula@corredora-test.cl\",\n  \"password\": \"corredora123\",\n  \"name\": \"Corredora Paula\",\n  \"whatsapp\": \"+56922222222\",\n  \"role\": \"CORREDORA\",\n  \"razonSocial\": \"Paula Propiedades SpA\",\n  \"rut\": \"22.222.222-2\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["users"] },
            "description": "Requiere estar logueado (correr 'Login (correcto)' primero). Guarda el id creado en {{publicadorId}} para usarlo al crear una propiedad. Si ya la corriste antes, va a dar 409 (email duplicado) — normal, la cuenta ya existe."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201 || pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('publicadorId', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "  console.log('publicadorId guardado:', pm.response.json().id);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Listar publicadores",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }] },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/users", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["users"] },
            "description": "Todas las cuentas PERSONA/CORREDORA (el admin no sale en esta lista)."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Uploads (Cloudinary)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Firma para subir foto/video",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }] },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/uploads/signature", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["uploads", "signature"] },
            "description": "Con las credenciales de prueba del .env, esto NO sube nada real a Cloudinary — solo prueba que el backend arma bien la firma. Con credenciales reales (cuenta free en cloudinary.com), esta respuesta es lo que el frontend necesita para subir un archivo directo a `https://api.cloudinary.com/v1_1/{cloudName}/auto/upload` (form-data: file, api_key, timestamp, signature, folder)."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Trae los 5 campos esperados', () => {",
                  "  ['cloudName','apiKey','timestamp','folder','signature'].forEach(k => pm.expect(body).to.have.property(k));",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Properties",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "1. Crear propiedad (queda BORRADOR)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"publicadorId\": \"{{publicadorId}}\",\n  \"tipoOperacion\": \"VENTA\",\n  \"tipoPropiedad\": \"CASA\",\n  \"comunaId\": \"{{comunaId}}\",\n  \"precioUf\": 3500,\n  \"dormitorios\": 3,\n  \"banos\": 2,\n  \"descripcion\": \"Casa de prueba con 3 dormitorios y buen patio en Melipilla.\"\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/properties", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["properties"] },
            "description": "Necesita {{publicadorId}} seteado (correr antes 'Crear corredora de prueba'). Toda propiedad nueva nace en estado BORRADOR — invisible en el catálogo público a propósito."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Nace en BORRADOR', () => pm.expect(body.estado).to.eql('BORRADOR'));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('propertyId', body.id);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('propertySlug', body.slug);",
                  "console.log('propertyId:', body.id, '| slug:', body.slug);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "2. Catálogo público (BORRADOR no debe aparecer)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/properties?comunaId={{comunaId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["properties"],
              "query": [{ "key": "comunaId", "value": "{{comunaId}}" }]
            },
            "description": "Sin token a propósito — es el endpoint que va a usar el sitio público. La propiedad recién creada NO debería salir acá todavía (sigue BORRADOR)."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "3. Ficha pública por slug (debe dar 404)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertySlug}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["properties", "{{propertySlug}}"] },
            "description": "Mismo motivo que el anterior: BORRADOR no es visible por slug tampoco."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": { "type": "text/javascript", "exec": ["pm.test('Devuelve 404 (todavia borrador)', () => pm.response.to.have.status(404));"] }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "4. Publicar (PATCH estado=PUBLICADA)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }] },
            "body": { "mode": "raw", "raw": "{\n  \"estado\": \"PUBLICADA\",\n  \"destacada\": true\n}" },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["properties", "{{propertyId}}"] },
            "description": "PATCH acepta solo los campos que mandás (UpdatePropertyDto es todo opcional) — acá solo cambiamos estado y destacada."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "5. Catálogo público de nuevo (ahora sí aparece)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/properties?comunaId={{comunaId}}",
              "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["properties"],
              "query": [{ "key": "comunaId", "value": "{{comunaId}}" }]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('Aparece al menos 1 propiedad', () => pm.expect(body.total).to.be.above(0));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "6. Listado admin (todas, cualquier estado)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }] },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/properties/admin/all", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["properties", "admin", "all"] },
            "description": "Protegido. Sin token da 401 — probalo sacando el Bearer Token de la pestaña Authorization."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "7. Asociar una foto (simulada, sin subir de verdad)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"cloudinaryPublicId\": \"market-propiedades/properties/test123\",\n  \"orden\": 0\n}"
            },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}/fotos", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["properties", "{{propertyId}}", "fotos"] },
            "description": "En la app real, `cloudinaryPublicId` sale de subir el archivo con la firma de 'Firma para subir foto/video'. Acá se manda un id inventado solo para probar que la relación PropertyFoto se arma bien."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('Devuelve 201', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('fotoId', pm.response.json().id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "8. Quitar la foto",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }] },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/properties/fotos/{{fotoId}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["properties", "fotos", "{{fotoId}}"] }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "9. Borrar propiedad de prueba",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "auth": { "type": "bearer", "bearer": [{ "key": "token", "value": "{{accessToken}}" }] },
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/properties/{{propertyId}}", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["properties", "{{propertyId}}"] },
            "description": "Limpieza — dejá el catálogo de prueba sin basura."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
